          "email": "yujian@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-28 07:50:26.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-21054 build: link the program in the mpitests check",
        "message": "LU-21054 build: link the program in the mpitests check\n\nLB_CONFIG_MPITESTS checks whether the MPI tests can be built with\nAC_COMPILE_IFELSE, so the test program is only compiled and never\nlinked. A broken MPI library passes the check, mpitests are enabled,\nand the build then fails when linking the programs in\nlustre/tests/mpi. Since mpitests are enabled by default with the\nmpicc found in PATH, this hits builds that did not ask for them.\n\nThis was seen on ARM64 clients with an OpenMPI whose libmpi.so has\na NEEDED entry for liblustreapi.so.1, which does not exist on the\nbuild node before Lustre is installed.\n\nLink the program in the check, so a broken MPI library disables\nmpitests at configure time instead of failing the build.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I9bac6f976022eb2f291dee595263fb214a7bf0d4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
